inspiration "joy-buolamwini" name="Joy Buolamwini" profile-citation="joy-buolamwini-ajl" impact-mode="public-advocacy" {
    achievement "Her Gender Shades research exposed major gender and skin-type performance disparities in commercial facial-analysis systems and helped establish algorithmic auditing as a public concern."
    impact-fit "Buolamwini creates impact by combining empirical research, art, and public advocacy to expose harmful technologies and build demand for accountability."
    appearance "fighting-bias-in-algorithms" title="How I'm Fighting Bias in Algorithms" event="TEDxBeaconStreet" year="2016" format="ted-talk" {
        summary """
            Buolamwini turns a facial-analysis system's failure to detect her face into an explanation of the assumptions and exclusions embedded in technical systems. Visual demonstrations and technical evidence make the failure visible onstage.

            The talk expresses her designer, playful, and public-advocacy assignments by making an invisible engineering problem emotionally and politically legible.
            """
        citation "joy-buolamwini-ted"
